---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SectionRule from '../components/composition/SectionRule.astro';
import Marginalia from '../components/composition/Marginalia.astro';
import { author } from '../data/author';

const mailto = `mailto:${author.email}?subject=Knowledge%20base%20setup`;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Work with me"
  description="AI knowledge base setup for growing companies. Fixed price, two-week delivery, full handover."
>
  <section class="wwm grid-cartesian">
    <h1 class="col-1-8 wwm-title">Your company's knowledge is scattered. Your AI should fix that.</h1>
    <p class="col-3-8 wwm-lede">
      I build private AI knowledge systems grounded in your company's actual documents and
      processes — so your team spends less time searching and more time executing. Fixed price,
      delivered in two weeks, yours to own.
    </p>
    <p class="col-3-8">
      <a class="wwm-cta" href={mailto}>Email me about your setup →</a>
    </p>

    <div class="col-1-12">
      <SectionRule align="start">The problem</SectionRule>
    </div>

    <dl class="col-1-8 wwm-rows">
      <div class="wwm-row">
        <dt>The answer exists. Finding it takes an hour.</dt>
        <dd>
          Processes, past decisions, client history — spread across six tools and three inboxes.
          Every search is a small tax on focus.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="wwm-row">
        <dt>Documents pile up. Knowledge doesn't.</dt>
        <dd>
          The documentation is there; when someone new joins, nobody knows where to start. The
          intelligence isn't.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="wwm-row">
        <dt>The same questions get answered over and over.</dt>
        <dd>
          Senior people field interruptions that could be self-served. Knowledge bottlenecks become
          people bottlenecks.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <div class="col-1-12">
      <SectionRule align="start">How it works</SectionRule>
    </div>

    <ol class="col-1-8 wwm-steps">
      <li>
        <span class="mono-caption">01 · Audit</span>
        I map where your knowledge lives, who owns it, and what's actually used. A few days, no
        workshops.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mono-caption">02 · Build</span>
        A private retrieval system (RAG) over your documents, connected to the tools you already
        use. Zero new habits required.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mono-caption">03 · Handover</span>
        Documentation, team training, full ownership. It runs without me; ongoing support is
        optional, never structural.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="col-1-12">
      <SectionRule align="start">The offer</SectionRule>
    </div>

    <div class="col-1-8 wwm-offer">
      <h2 class="wwm-offer-title">AI knowledge base setup</h2>
      <p class="wwm-offer-meta mono-caption">€4,500 · delivered in 2 weeks · fixed scope</p>
      <p>
        A working retrieval system over your documents and SOPs — ingestion, hybrid retrieval,
        grounded answers — integrated where your team already works, handed over completely. If one
        senior person spends four hours a week on internal search, the setup pays for itself in
        about three months.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="wwm-cta" href={mailto}>Email me — I'll reply with three scoping questions →</a>
      </p>
      <p class="wwm-also">
        Also available: larger document-intelligence pipelines (analysis and extraction at volume)
        and an optional monthly support retainer — ask if either fits.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="col-1-12">
      <SectionRule align="start">Who builds this</SectionRule>
    </div>

    <div class="col-1-8 wwm-about">
      <p>
        I'm {author.shortName} — an AI engineer working on RAG systems, document intelligence, and
        LLM integration. Background: M.S. Robotics at EPFL; perception engineer at Roboat (MIT
        spinoff), where I shipped production ML on real hardware; currently research fellow at MIT
        Senseable City Lab, leading a ten-person technical team. I take a small number of client
        projects at a time.
      </p>
      <p>
        No testimonials on this page yet — I don't publish social proof I can't stand behind. I'll
        show you real work on a call, under NDA where needed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="col-1-12">
      <SectionRule align="start">Questions</SectionRule>
    </div>

    <dl class="col-1-8 wwm-rows">
      <div class="wwm-row">
        <dt>We tried AI tools and the team stopped using them.</dt>
        <dd>
          Generic tools fail because they aren't built around how your team works. This is grounded
          in your content, wired into your existing tools, and scoped to your workflows — not
          another tab.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="wwm-row">
        <dt>Are we dependent on you afterwards?</dt>
        <dd>
          No. Every project ends with documentation, a handover session, and full ownership.
          Dependency is a design flaw.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="wwm-row">
        <dt>Is this a ChatGPT wrapper?</dt>
        <dd>
          The model matters less than the retrieval architecture, data quality, and integration.
          You're paying for a system that knows your company, on your data, privately.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <div class="col-1-8 wwm-close">
      <p class="wwm-close-line">Your knowledge is an asset. Let's make it work.</p>
      <p><a class="wwm-cta" href={mailto}>{author.email} →</a></p>
    </div>

    <aside class="col-10-12 wwm-margin">
      <Marginalia voice="mono">
        One email is enough to find out whether this fits. I'll tell you honestly if it doesn't.
      </Marginalia>
    </aside>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .wwm {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) var(--space-section);
    row-gap: var(--s-6);
  }
  .wwm-title {
    font-family: var(--font-cartesian);
    font-size: var(--text-display-lg);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    max-width: 20ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .wwm-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--text-body-lg);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }
  .wwm-cta {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      color 200ms ease,
      border-color 200ms ease;
  }
  .wwm-cta:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .wwm-rows {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .wwm-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 1fr) 2fr;
    gap: var(--s-6);
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: var(--s-4) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }
  .wwm-row dt {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .wwm-row dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
  .wwm-steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-6);
  }
  .wwm-steps li {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .wwm-offer {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .wwm-offer-title {
    font-family: var(--font-cartesian);
    font-size: var(--text-display-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .wwm-offer-meta {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .wwm-offer p,
  .wwm-about p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .wwm-also {
    font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }
  .wwm-about {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .wwm-close {
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }
  .wwm-close-line {
    font-family: var(--font-cartesian);
    font-size: var(--text-display-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 24ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .wwm-margin {
    align-self: end;
    padding-bottom: var(--s-6);
  }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .wwm-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--s-1);
    }
  }
</style>
